    "reason": "The busy-timeout save, set and restore of main's hermes_state.py::SessionDB._read_ctx run with the caller's lock wait in place of _READ_BUSY_TIMEOUT_S, because in main the reads that use it opened connections of their own with their own wait: 2 s in hermes_cli/worktree_ops.py::_tree_still_served and hermes_cli/worktree_ops.py::_retained_tree_is_live, 0.05 s in tui_gateway/change_watcher.py::_session_db_content_sig, and 10 s in tools/async_delegation.py::_connect and gateway/delivery_ledger.py::_connect. The backend runs the three statements inside its own _read_ctx block, so they are labelled read, while main runs them in _read_ctx's body, which no caller in main nests in another read, so they are labelled none."
   }
